# Everything is LF, in the index and in the working tree, on every OS.
#
# This repo is written on Linux and applied on Windows. PowerShell 7, Windows
# Terminal, VS Code, git and Docker Desktop all read LF files without complaint,
# so CRLF buys nothing - while Git for Windows' installer default
# (core.autocrlf=true) would rewrite every file on checkout and turn the first
# commit made from the other OS into a whole-repo diff.
#
# NB: keep the .ps1 files ASCII. Anything that ends up in Windows PowerShell 5.1
# (powershell.exe) reads a UTF-8 file without a BOM in the ANSI code page, so a
# single em dash or curly quote becomes mojibake - or a parse error when it lands
# inside a string.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.ico   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary

docs/*.md linguist-documentation
